# Entity and state language

A domain is a family of entities, such as `light`. A device class says more, such as a door sensor. A state is the value Home Assistant holds. Attributes add related facts. None of these proves that someone checked the device or that an action finished.

Use the entity’s own label and the name someone gave it. Add the domain, device class, unit and time when they help. Do not replace a precise state with a general “on”, “off”, “failed” or “offline”.

