## Know what each kind of value is

| Kind | Example | How to use it |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Entity ID | `light.nains_reading_lamp` | A full ID. Use the real ID from the household’s setup |
| Domain | `light` | A family of entities. Not a full entity ID |
| Raw state | `on` | Read it with its domain and device class |
| Attribute property | `hvac_action` | A key inside the state. Not an entity ID |
| Attribute value | `heating` | The value of one attribute. Not the same as a selected mode |
| Device-class key | `door` | Names the label for that class in that domain |
| Default translation key | `_` | A default entry in a translation file. Do not copy it anywhere |

The tables below show English labels so you can identify an entry. They are not new translations. Home Assistant picks the language. Some integrations supply their own values, and those are not listed.

